      "value": "@{60e65f577ae9d0492b0f2a75|full_name}: Thank you for providing more information. After some investigation, it appears that the specific issue you are running into is that the update has made the \"shortname\" field a requirement regardless of whether or not you would otherwise have permission to join the instance, which means that only instances generated by the VRChat API directly are valid. I will have to get back to you on whether or not this is intended, as it could be a security measure of some kind or it could just be a bug. Regardless, if you just need something to work in the meantime, then the solution is to use the VRChat website to generate your instance links rather than generating them manually or with the VRCQuickLauncher.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
